<!--
  The mark on the layer a launcher masks.

  A launcher draws this in a box of 108 units and is only obliged to show the middle 66 of
  them, and the farthest thing in the drawing from its own centre is the corner of the frame,
  49.4975 of the drawing's 100 units away. The drawing is therefore scaled by 66/98.9949 and
  centred, which puts the whole mark inside that circle. Scaling it to the 72-unit square
  instead leaves the frame's corners outside the circle, where a mask with round corners cuts
  them off and the icon reads as a drawing running off its own tile.

  The plate is part of the drawing and is the same color as the background layer, so on a
  masked launcher the two are one surface.

  The gamepad inside the frame is the Material Symbols `stadia_controller` glyph, whose own
  box runs from x 42 to 919 and y -960 to -160. The group below scales it to 36 units wide
  and places it above and left of the frame's centre: the frame's bottom right corner is
  chamfered, so a glyph centred at 50,50 would cross that chamfer. The glyph's two subpaths
  are kept as one path, which is how the manufacturer cuts its inner outline out.
-->
